{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Rotation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Object Rotation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"object rotation object rotation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Object Rotation.md","fileName":"Object Rotation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Object Rotation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D Manipulation","Input Device","Clutching","Feedback","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Rotation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Object Rotation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"object rotation object rotation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Object Rotation.md","fileName":"Object Rotation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Object Rotation","heading":"Object Rotation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Object rotation changes an object's orientation. It is a canonical [[3D Manipulation]] task whose difficulty depends on the initial and target orientations, the amount of rotation, distance to the object, and required precision.\n\nAn [[Input Device]] that integrates rotational degrees of freedom can support coordinated movement, but its grip and range matter. A precision grip can use smaller finger muscles for fine rotation, while a limited hand or device range may force [[Clutching]].\n\nDirectionally compliant [[Feedback]] makes the virtual object rotate in the same direction as the physical control, helping the user predict the result.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D Manipulation","Input Device","Clutching","Feedback","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Rotat